-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, four amphibious and naval craft (printed 186-192): Crocodile amphibious tank, Crayfish amphibious submersible, Harbormaster missile boat, Sandfish cargo landing craft
-- 4 vehicle rows, with 35 locations and 12 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~320-northern-gun-2-aquatic-b.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-amp8-crocodile-tank', 'NG-AMP8 Crocodile Amphibious Tank', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Two: a driver and a gunner.', 'Room for two.', '70 mph (112 km) maximum on flat ground such as roads, grassland or desert; 25-35 mph (40 to 56 km) through brush and sparse forest. Moderate or dense forest stops it.', NULL, '25 mph (40 km) maximum on the surface; 15 mph (24 km or 13 knots) partially submerged.', 'Height 9 ft (2.7 m); width 11 ft (3.3 m); length 30 ft (9.1 m)', '28 tons with a full weapons load', 340, 1, NULL, 2700000, '5 million credits nuclear (about 12 years), 4 million Solid Oxide, 2.7 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model NG-AMP8 (Class: Amphibious Armored Vehicle). A low, light tank from the team of Magnar Laksa, Brian Lindholm and Sean Jenkins that drives on land, floats like a boat and can sit two-thirds under the water with only its turret and the front of the crew compartment showing, where it passes for floating wreckage. That lets it patrol unseen and come up out of the shallows straight onto a beach; all three of its weapon systems work on land, afloat and half sunk. It runs on eight wheels rather than tracks, their treads helping the rear and belly water jets push it along. Instead of a tank gun it carries a laser cannon, an ion blaster and four short-range missiles at the back, which serve against armour and also for shelling shore defences and patrol boats. Around the Great Lakes it suits land-bound mercenary companies and town defenders, since it can cross any lake, river or small sea in its way. Cargo: little beyond two NG-S2 Survival Kits plus personal arms for the crew. Sensors: standard, as robot vehicles.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.186-187'),
  ('ng-su7-crayfish-sub', 'NG-SU7 Crayfish Amphibious Submersible', 'rifts', 'ship', 'Three: a pilot, a gunner and a communications engineer.', 'Six, wearing man-sized power armor or heavy diving suits.', '35 mph (56 km) on dry land; 5 mph (8 km) crawling on its treads along a lake or sea floor.', NULL, 'Surface 20 mph (32 km); underwater 25 mph (40 km), usually 2-8 mph (3.2 to 13 km) when searching for salvage. Maximum depth 2.5 miles (4 km).', 'Height 12 ft (3.6 m); width 16 ft (4.9 m); length 28 ft (8.5 m)', '26 tons', 280, 1, NULL, 6500000, '10 million credits nuclear (about 12 years), 8 million Solid Oxide, 6.5 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model NG-SU7 (Class: Amphibious Exploration and Salvage Submersible). A small, blocky submarine from Michael Macolley, Jeff Jensen and Mike Creelman that also floats on the surface, crawls along the bottom and climbs out onto dry land on a pair of tank treads that fold down from its sides and lock up again when not wanted. Small enough to slip past most naval patrols, it hides in shallow rivers, lakes, coastal pools and marshes, and can leave one body of water, cross land and enter another. Harbor patrols, salvage crews, pirates, privateers, spies, mercenaries and adventurers use it. Two folding robot arms at the front, with clamp-like hands made for lifting rather than fighting, gather salvage, shift debris and grab passing ships to ride along. Pirates favour a two-part raid: those on the surface heave a victim''s crates overboard and the Crayfish collects them from the bottom, then carries them by water or overland to waiting trucks or boats; the Black Market keeps buyers waiting for such goods. If its rudder or propeller fails, it simply drops to the bottom and drives home. Treads: losing one set cuts crawling speed by 80%, costs -20% piloting and leaves a plain trail (a silt cloud underwater); losing both stops it on land or the bottom. Windows are for observation only, so sealing them changes nothing for the pilot; losing both glass and plate floods the sub. Cargo: about 4 tons inside and 4 more lashed on top (-20% speed, -10% piloting, and a failed roll loses the load); each arm holds 2 tons or pulls 6 more (-10% speed, -5% piloting). Robot P.S. 34. Sensors: standard, as robot vehicles, plus passive sonar tracking 20 targets to 5 miles (8 km) unnoticed and active sonar to 25 miles (40 km), which reveals it. Lights: the forward lights in the tread-housing noses swivel 25 degrees and the belly lights light the water below for divers, both to 600 ft (183 m); light draws predators, and infrared is useless since many sea creatures see it.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.187-189'),
  ('ng-s3-harbormaster-missile-boat', 'NG-S3 Harbormaster Missile Boat', 'rifts', 'ship', 'Three: a pilot/captain, a navigator/sensor operator and a gunner.', 'Two passengers, plus six jet-pack troopers in EBA, or four in power armor: usually the Blue Hawk, Red Hawk or another flying suit, though the Beach-Stormer or any armor suited to the job will do.', NULL, NULL, '55 mph (88 km) maximum on the surface. It cannot submerge.', 'Height 14 ft (4.3 m) with the netting; width 16 ft (4.9 m); length 32 ft (9.8 m)', '10 tons fully loaded', 275, 1, NULL, 870000, '2.2 million credits nuclear (about 12 years), 1.6 million Solid Oxide, 1 million electric battery, 870,000 liquid fuel; the lowest is stored. Sold with a full load of short-range missiles and two inflatable lifeboats.', 'Model NG-S3 (Class: Light Missile Boat). Northern Gun''s main small attack craft: far smaller than a full patrol boat but quick and heavily armed, with short-range missiles in place of torpedoes so it can engage aircraft and shore targets and not only vessels on the Great Lakes or the open sea. Three features are borrowed from bigger ships. Its blue-green laser runs on a rail along the keel, sliding fore and aft under the water to meet enemies or incoming torpedoes, or up out of the water as a second surface gun. A recovery net at the stern slows and catches returning jet pack and flying power armor troops so they land without going overboard. And it carries a small flight of marines, in EBA with jet packs or in flying armor (the Blue Hawk is standard), used much as an aircraft carrier once used its helicopters: scouting, quick response, interception and hunting submarines. Fast and with eyes overhead, it serves for harbor security, patrols, escort, hit-and-run raids, search and rescue, guarding long stretches of lake, boarding ships and air-to-water or water-to-land raids. Cargo: a 5x5 ft (1.5 x 1.5 m) locker for weapons, gear or a stowed power armor suit, two inflatable lifeboats and four small fold-out bunks. Sensors: standard, as robot vehicles, plus passive sonar tracking 48 targets to 5 miles (8 km) unnoticed, active sonar to 25 miles (40 km), which gives its position away, and a built-in loudspeaker.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.190-191'),
  ('ng-s1-sandfish-landing-craft', 'NG-S1 Sandfish Cargo Landing Craft', 'rifts', 'ship', 'Four: a pilot, a navigator/sensor operator and two gunners.', 'Supply runs usually add 8-12 ordinary workers to unload, or 1-2 in exoskeletons or power armor; troops and vehicles ride as cargo.', '2 mph (3.2 km), and only over fairly level, clear, smooth ground.', NULL, '40 mph (64 km) maximum.', 'Height 19 ft (5.8 m); width 22 ft (6.7 m); length 70 ft (21 m)', '26 tons empty', 400, 1, NULL, 750000, '1.5 million credits nuclear (about 12 years), 1.2 million Solid Oxide, 750,000 electric battery or liquid fuel; the lowest is stored.', 'Model NG-S1 (Class: Landing Craft Cargo Hauler and Troop Transport). A cargo boat after the pattern of the World War II landing craft, proposed by the team of Craig Hammer, Benjamin Bonds and Melissa Powell, for buyers who will take delivery on the beach: it runs up to the shore and drops a big bow ramp. It serves as a ferry for people and vehicles, or hauls cargo, ore and raw materials, troops, vehicles, giant robots and war supplies, and needs no port or dock, only a reasonably flat beach. A tank-like drive track under the waterline lets it climb over reefs, sandbars, sand and rocks; too big and clumsy for real land travel, it can still creep across dry ground between waters and sometimes pass from a Great Lake into a river or a smaller lake. A support craft, not a warship, short on speed, armour and guns, but sturdy in the Northern Gun way and not stopped by bad weather or rough going, so merchants, exporters, haulers, explorers and adventurers like it. Cargo: up to 96 tons, with one small cabin holding a bed and four fold-out crew bunks. Sensors: standard, as robot vehicles.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.191-192');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicle_locations (vehicle_slug, location, mdc, mdc_note, ordinal) VALUES
  ('ng-amp8-crocodile-tank', 'Turret (1, top)', 120, 'Depleted, it knocks out the laser cannon and the smoke dispensers; the spotlight and the ion blaster keep working.', 1),
